<title>ITALY: Italy metalworkers unions and employers meet.</title>
<headline>Italy metalworkers unions and employers meet.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leaders of Italy's main unions were holding talks with the director general of the federation of Italian metalworkers, Federmeccanica, on Monday in an unscheduled meeting, a union source said.</p>
<p>The union official said the leaders of Italy's three main union federations, the Cigl, Cisl and Uil, along with the leaders of the three metalworkers' unions, the Fim, Fiom and Uilm, met Federmeccanica's Michele Figurati.</p>
<p>Employers' chiefs expressed cautious optimism last week that a solution might soon be found to the long running pay dispute in the metalworkers' and engineering sector. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
